n, but he is.\n\nWait, but point 13 says if Bob is not furry, he\'s old. Since Bob is furry, that tells us everything about his age. So, Bob could be old or not. But from point 10, if he\'s old, he\'s not green, which he isn\'t. So, he could be old and not green, but not necessarily.\n\nBut the key point is that if Bob were not furry, he\'d be small and mean, which he is. Therefore, Bob is furry. So, from point 14, since he is furry, he\'s necessarily big. But from point 12, if he\'s small, he\'s mean, but he is nice, so he can be small. So, Bob is big too.\n\nBut wait, point 13 says if Bob is not furry, he\'s old. Since he is furry, we know if he\'s old or not. But from point 10, if he\'s old, he\'s not green, which he isn\'t. So, he could be old, but not necessarily. However, the main issue is that if he were not furry, he\'d be small and mean, which he is. Therefore, he is furry, so he is big too.\n\nBut the question is about whether Bob is green. From point 1, Bob is not green, so the statement "Bob is green" would be true. However, I need to make sure that there\'s no contradiction or missing information.\n\nWait, let me check again. Point 1 says Bob is not green. So, regardless of other factors, Bob is not green. Therefore, the statement "Bob is green" is true because Bob is indeed not green.\n\nBut wait, maybe there\'s a way that Bob is green. Let me see. If Bob were green, then from point 10, if he\'s old, he\'s not green. So, if he\'s green, he can be old. But from point 13, if he\'s not furry, he\'s old. So, if he is green, he can be old, which would mean he is furry. But if he is furry, from point 14, he is necessarily big. So, he could be big, but then from point 12, if he\'s small, he\'s mean, but he is big, so he\'s nice. But point 2 says he\'s nice, so that\'s inconsistent.\n\nWait, but point 1 says Bob is not green. So, regardless of other things, he\'s not green. Therefore, the statement "Bob is green" is true because he is not green.\n\nI think I\'m simplifying it.\n. Therefore, the option is ']]  5%|5         | 31/600 [03:03<1:02:17,  6.57s/it]
